# The compiled signage assets in screenly-cast/assets/dist/ are deliberately
# COMMITTED: WordPress.org ships no build step, so the plugin has to carry its
# own built CSS/JS. CI verifies they match a fresh build.

# Generated by `bun run readme` from readme/*.md and the GitHub releases. Not
# committed, unlike the compiled assets above, and the difference is that these are
# not reproducible from the repository alone: the changelog comes from release notes,
# which can be edited after the fact. A committed copy would drift the moment anyone
# fixed a typo in a release, and a drift check that fails for reasons outside the
# repository is a check people learn to ignore. The reviewable source is readme/.
/screenly-cast/readme.txt
/screenly-cast/changelog.txt
